  "discussions_data": [
    {
      "id": "a7f0498c5ea638bddc86e7aa533d2933588d3720",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1272766175,
          "type": null,
          "body": "I am realizing that my intuition for bit ordering was wrong. The RFC has this figure:\n```\n                                 0 1 2 3 4 5 6 7\n                                +-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+\n                                |PC1|PC2|PC3|PC4|\n                                +-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+\n```\nwhich I interpreted using the following masks:\n```\n#define RPL_OPT_TRANSIT_PATHCTL_PC1     0x03\n#define RPL_OPT_TRANSIT_PATHCTL_PC2     0x0C\n#define RPL_OPT_TRANSIT_PATHCTL_PC3     0x30\n#define RPL_OPT_TRANSIT_PATHCTL_PC4     0xC0\n```\nbut it turns out it is the other way around (as described in [RFC 791 Appendix B](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc791#page-39)).\n\nI made the same mistake in my previous pull request on ND-EARO (commmit `7908dfd9`).\nI will add a fixup for this previous patch, but I can remove it from this pull request and open a new one if it is more suited.",
          "author": {
            "id": 10365825,
            "username": "MathisMARION",
            "public_email": null,
            "name": "Mathis MARION",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/c410127f4b082d0a3b0d505350206a1c97720c93ec2b2820ca14a9b2f888cb6c?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/MathisMARION"
          },
          "created_at": "2023-02-09T17:35:22.737Z",
          "updated_at": "2023-02-10T12:33:02.370Z",
          "system": false,
